REMARK 400                                                                      
REMARK 400 COMPOUND                                                             
REMARK 400 THIS MODEL IS THAT OF THE H134A MUTANT AT 2.0 ANGSTROMS.             
REMARK 400 THREE NONIDENTICAL CHAINS, GAMMA (A), BETA (B), AND ALPHA            
REMARK 400 (C) FORM ONE (ABC)-UNIT.  THE ASYMMETRIC UNIT CONTAINS ONE           
REMARK 400 (ABC)-UNIT.                                                          
REMARK 400 RESIDUES 317 - 331 OF THE MOBILE ACTIVE SITE FLAP IN CHAIN           
REMARK 400 C ARE SUFFICIENTLY DISORDERED THAT THEY WERE NOT MODELED             
REMARK 400 NI2 IS NOT PRESENT DUE TO THE LOSS OF THE NICKEL LIGAND              
REMARK 400 HIS 134.  NI1 IS NOW LIGATED BY THREE WATER MOLECULES                
REMARK 400 (WATERS 176, 177, AND 179) WHICH ALONG WITH THREE PROTEIN            
REMARK 400 LIGANDS FORM AN OCTAHEDRAL COORDINATION GEOMETRY FOR NI1.            
